BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 222.55 Tm (defective, every other measurement doesn't matter whatsoever. The check is to clip to the 1 ohm stud,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 207.33 Tm (select earth resistance, and expect a reading that stabilizes near 1 ohm. All metals oxidize at the surface) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 192.10 Tm (layer, so a high reading means rotating the clamp to break through [HBf8beE8tGc @ 00:00:49]. The current) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 176.88 Tm (side gets verified on the 100 microamp stud in enclosure leakage mode, where the result came in off by 0.5) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 161.65 Tm (of a microamp [HBf8beE8tGc @ 00:01:39]. AbishkarTECH shows what a bad supply looks like on screen: a) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 146.43 Tm (no-ground fault. Live-to-neutral read a correct 225, but live-to-earth read 53 when it should have matched,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 131.20 Tm (and neutral-to-earth read 32 against an expected figure under five [rqUE2pFiqUI @ 00:00:44]. That same) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 115.98 Tm (ground fault and a loose connection pushed protective earth to 0.062 against roughly 0.03, even after the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 100.75 Tm (leads were zeroed [rqUE2pFiqUI @ 00:02:03]. Better Biomed Channel zeros leads on the SA 2600 because) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 85.53 Tm (leads carry inherent resistance, then flexes the cord at both ends during the ground read [6JXtlTgXvKo @) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 70.30 Tm (00:01:40]. Skipping lead and supply verification puts every downstream pass or fail in doubt.) Tj ET
